        <history>
          <p>Written as a companion piece to ‘On Hearing the First Cuckoo in Spring’, this evocation of a quiet river at night shares the same pair of Norwegian folk-song sources. The two works are almost always performed together and are considered among the finest examples of Delius's impressionistic orchestral writing, prizing atmosphere and slowly shifting harmony over conventional development.</p>
